@startuml power-domains
' LocalAiRobot — DETAILED power domains + signal wiring (camera, face & 3-sensor array).
' This source lives next to its render. Regenerate in place (writes power-domains.png here):
'   plantuml -tpng docs/images/power-domains.puml
' No Graphviz needed: !pragma layout smetana uses PlantUML's pure-Java layout engine.
' Grouped like assembly.puml: each battery domain is one labelled box; PCA9685 + GND bus sit between.
!pragma layout smetana
hide stereotype
title LocalAiRobot — detailed power domains (never bridge the batteries) + sensors, camera & face

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  FontSize 12
  BorderThickness 1
  BackgroundColor<<io>> #DAE8FC
  BorderColor<<io>> #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<model>> #FFF2CC
  BorderColor<<model>> #D6B656
  BackgroundColor<<data>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<data>> #82B366
  BackgroundColor<<motor>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<motor>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #F5F5F5
  BorderColor<<store>> #666666
  BackgroundColor<<motordomain>> #FBEAEA
  BorderColor<<motordomain>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<braindomain>> #E6EEF8
  BorderColor<<braindomain>> #6C8EBF
}

' ---- brain domain: Pi power + everything the Pi drives directly ----
rectangle "Brain power  (UPS HAT  —  or 27W PSU for bench bring-up)" as brainbox <<braindomain>> {
  rectangle "UPS HAT (2x 18650)\nor official 27W PSU (bench)" as ups <<io>>
  rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n+ Active Cooler (mandatory)" as pi <<io>>
  rectangle "HC-SR04P x3  (3.3V; no divider)\nfront 23/24  •  left 5/6  •  right 20/21" as sonar <<data>>
  rectangle "Pi Camera V2 NoIR\n(IMX219, CSI via 22->15 adapter)" as cam <<data>>
  rectangle "Face screen\n(USB-C -> /dev/ttyACM0)" as face <<io>>
}
ups --> pi : 5V to Pi
pi --> sonar : 3.3V + TRIG/ECHO
pi --> cam : CSI ribbon
pi --> face : USB-C (serial)

' ---- motor domain: LiPo high-current path (servo power stays in here) ----
rectangle "Motor power  (LiPo, high current)" as motorbox <<motordomain>> {
  rectangle "2S 7.4V LiPo" as lipo <<motor>>
  rectangle "ESC\n(battery input + 7.4V/2A BEC)" as esc <<motor>>
  rectangle "drive motor" as dmotor <<motor>>
  rectangle "steering servo\n(DS3225 HV, on the 7.4V BEC rail)" as servo <<motor>>
}
lipo --> esc : 7.4 V
esc --> dmotor : motor drive

' ---- the only places the two domains legitimately meet: 3.3V logic/PWM signals + common GND ----
rectangle "PCA9685\n(I2C PWM bridge, 0x40)" as pca <<model>>
rectangle "common GND bus\n(Pi <-> PCA9685 <-> ESC)" as gnd <<store>>

pi  --> pca   : 3.3V logic (VCC) + I2C SDA/SCL
esc --> pca   : ch0 throttle PWM (signal)
esc --> pca   : 7.4V/2A BEC -> V+ rail (servo power, LiPo domain)
pca --> servo : ch1: 7.4V + PWM

esc ..> gnd : GND
pi  ..> gnd : GND
pca ..> gnd : GND

note bottom of gnd
  **Never bridge LiPo + and UPS/PSU +.** The domains meet ONLY at shared **GND** and the 3.3V logic / PWM signals.
  The **ESC 7.4V BEC -> PCA9685 V+ rail** is internal to the LiPo/motor domain (servo power), NOT a bridge to the Pi.
  **7.4V BEC = use an HV servo, or feed V+ from a separate 5-6V BEC** (a 6V-only servo can be damaged).
  Bench bring-up: power the Pi from the **27W PSU first** (UPS later). DS3225 stall ~2.5-3A — a 2A BEC may
  brown out under hard steering; add a separate servo BEC on V+ if so. All 3 HC-SR04**P** are 3.3V (ECHO Pi-safe).
end note
@enduml
